# Sanctuary Wall: the tap and the counter are separate instructions (CR 701.26a, 122.1d): a creature that is already tapped is no
# illegal target and, if its controller's opponent accepts, still gets the stun counter, so the Wall gets one too. Bot1 cast the
# Wall on turn 1 and holds Black Lotus; on turn 4 Bot2's Ornithopter attacks (tapped by attacking) and Bot1 activates the Wall at it
# in the declare attackers step and accepts: both have a stun counter, the Ornithopter still tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Sanctuary Wall
Black Lotus
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sanctuary Wall.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Sanctuary Wall.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
? Stack.Count = 0
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Counters.Stun = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Sanctuary Wall.Counters.Stun = 1

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
